 "text": "Hey, good to have you here. How are you? That's a common problem. It's because we' drawn from life, rather than drawn from life, and our eyes end up too big. A simple fix is to lower the eyes slightly. Not too low, just enough so the eyelid doesn't look like it's wide open. You can use a little bit of shadow under the eye too, to make it look more three dimensional. Yes, give each nostril a little line connecting it to the eye. It gives the nose a lot more depth. Fun to draw from life, or from a photo?",
